# apps/web/.vercelignore — the deployment root's ignore file.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS AND NOT ONLY THE ONE AT THE REPOSITORY ROOT.
#
# Vercel reads `.vercelignore` from the DEPLOYMENT ROOT, which is whatever the
# project's "Root Directory" setting points at. This project sets Root Directory
# to `apps/web` (see docs/03-system-design/RUNBOOK-deploy-vercel.md §2), so THIS
# file is the one that applies and `../../.vercelignore` is not.
#
# That was the open caveat written into the repository-root file: it warned that
# it would stop applying if the root were ever set to `apps/web`, and left the
# question there. It is settled now — the root IS `apps/web`, deliberately, and
# both files say so. Do not delete either one without reading the other.
#
# Most of what the root file excluded (docs/, war-room/, guides/, .agent/,
# .claude/, root *.png) is already outside `apps/web` and therefore already
# outside the upload. This file only has to deal with what is INSIDE apps/web
# and is not an input to the build.
#
# UNVERIFIED, and it matters: `.vercelignore` is documented for the file upload
# a CLI deploy performs. Whether it also prunes the working tree of a Git-
# integration build has not been tested by anyone on this project — nobody has
# deployed this configuration yet. Treat the entries below as a size and
# hygiene measure, never as a security boundary. Nothing secret is kept out of
# a deployment by this file; nothing secret is in the repository at all.

# Playwright end-to-end suite and its config. Never imported by the build —
# `next build` compiles from app/, components/ and lib/ only.
e2e/
playwright.config.ts

# Vitest config. Same reason.
vitest.config.ts

# The SQL schema. Applied to Supabase by a human from the dashboard or the
# Supabase CLI (RUNBOOK-deploy-vercel.md §4), never by the Next.js build. No
# module imports this directory.
supabase/

# Test and browser-automation output. Local artefacts; also gitignored, listed
# here so a stray local run cannot be uploaded by a CLI deploy.
coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/
.playwright/

# NOT excluded, deliberately:
#   __tests__/   — colocated under lib/ and app/. Left in the upload because
#                  nobody has verified that no shipping module reaches into one
#                  for a fixture, and a wrong guess here is a broken build on
#                  the founder's first deploy rather than a saved megabyte.
#   public/      — every byte of it is served, including the two ~6 MB PNGs the
#                  service-worker build already warns about (see §7).
